@startuml service-topology
!pragma teoz true
title Service Topology — {{System}}

' Derived from context-map.puml. Produced ONLY when the project is going microservice.
'   A service is a DEPLOYABLE unit. Default: one bounded context = one service.
'   Co-deploying contexts (modular monolith) is valid; NEVER split a context across services.
'   Each service owns its datastore — no shared DB across services.
'   Transport is DERIVED from the context-map pattern, not invented:
'     OHS+PL / Customer-Supplier / Conformist  -> synchronous (REST/gRPC)
'     Domain event crossing a context boundary -> integration event on a broker (async)
'     Anticorruption Layer                      -> translation adapter at the consumer edge
'     Separate Ways                             -> no integration

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<core>>        LightYellow
  BackgroundColor<<supporting>>  White
  BackgroundColor<<generic>>     WhiteSmoke
  BackgroundColor<<mud>>         MistyRose
  BorderColor<<core>>            GoldenRod
  BorderColor<<mud>>             Crimson
  BorderThickness<<core>>        2
  BorderThickness<<mud>>         2
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
  BorderColor Gray
}
skinparam ArrowColor Black
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor White

' --- Services: one deployable per bounded context by default ---
' Stereotype = subdomain type of the hosted context. Owner label = team.
rectangle "Orders Service\n(owns: Sales context)\nowner: Checkout team"        as Orders    <<core>>
rectangle "Catalog Service\n(owns: Catalog context)\nowner: PIM team"          as Catalog   <<supporting>>
rectangle "Inventory Service\n(owns: Inventory context)\nowner: Fulfilment team" as Inventory <<supporting>>
rectangle "Billing Service\n(owns: Billing context)\nowner: Payments team"     as Billing   <<supporting>>
rectangle "Legacy ERP Service\n(contains: Big Ball of Mud)"                   as ERP       <<mud>>

' --- Datastore ownership: one DB per service, never shared across services ---
database "Orders DB"    as OrdersDB
database "Catalog DB"   as CatalogDB
database "Inventory DB" as InventoryDB
database "Billing DB"   as BillingDB

Orders    --> OrdersDB    : owns
Catalog   --> CatalogDB   : owns
Inventory --> InventoryDB : owns
Billing   --> BillingDB   : owns

' --- Transport — DERIVED from the context-map pattern ---
' Solid black  = synchronous (REST/gRPC).  Dashed royal-blue = async (integration event on a broker).
' Dashed crimson = ACL translation adapter at the consuming edge.

' Billing is a Customer (D) of Orders (U): sync call to the supplier's OHS.
Orders    --> Billing    : sync (REST, OHS+PL)

' Inventory reacts to OrderPlaced as an INTEGRATION EVENT (async, eventual consistency).
Orders    -[#royalblue,dashed]-> Inventory : async\n(OrderPlaced -> ReserveStock)

' ACL at the Orders edge shields it from the messy legacy ERP model.
ERP       -[#crimson,dashed]-> "D (ACL)" Orders : sync via ACL\n(translates legacy model)

' --- Patterns not used in this example — copy/paste when needed ---
' Co-deployed contexts (modular monolith): one service box hosting several contexts.
'   rectangle "Commerce Service\n(owns: Sales + Catalog contexts)\nowner: Commerce team" as Commerce <<core>>
' Separate Ways: draw NO line — independence is the point.

legend right
  |= Line style |= Transport |
  | <color:#000000>────►</color>        | Synchronous (REST / gRPC) — OHS+PL, Customer–Supplier, Conformist |
  | <color:royalblue>─ ─ ►</color>      | Asynchronous (integration event on a broker) |
  | <color:crimson>─ ─ ►</color>        | Anticorruption Layer (translation at the consumer edge) |
  | (none)                              | Separate Ways — no integration |
  |--
  Each service owns its datastore (no shared DB across services).
  Service box color = subdomain type of the hosted context:
  <back:LightYellow> </back> Core · <back:White> </back> Supporting · <back:WhiteSmoke> </back> Generic · <back:MistyRose> </back> Big Ball of Mud
endlegend

@enduml
